<title>FINLAND: Nokia op cash flow still positive in H1.</title>
<headline>Nokia op cash flow still positive in H1.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications major Nokia Oy said on Monday its operating cash flow remained positive in the first half of the year.</p>
<p>&quot;It gives me great pleasure to note that cash flow from operations for the first half of the year was positive at FIM 4.2 billion,&quot; Nokia CEO Jorma Ollila said in the company's interim report.</p>
<p>Nokia reported strong growth, with group net sales up 45 percent year-on-year at 24.39 billion markka in the first half.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 248, news@reuters.fi</p>
